    "lawCode": "Amd §1263, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8833\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the residence\nof a certain non-voting member of the metropolitan transportation\nauthority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would allow the alternate non-voting member of the authority\nrecommended by the labor organizations representing the majority of\nemployees of the Metro-North Commuter Railroad Company to be a resident\nof any State that the Metro-North Commuter Railroad Company operates.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends subparagraph 2 of paragraph (a) of subdivision 1 of\nsection 2 1263 of the public authorities law, as amended by chapter 549\nof the 3 laws of 1994 to allow for the alternate non-voting member\nrecommended by the labor organization representing the majority of the\nemployees of the Metro-North Commuter Railroad Company to be a resident\nof any state in which the Metro-North Commuter Railroad Company oper-\nates.\n\nSection two sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDue to residency requirements under the current statute, the non-voting\nmember for labor organizations allowed to serve in this capacity is not\neligible due to residency requirements. This bill will ensure that the\nnonvoting member of the authority recommended by the labor organization\nis a resident of a state where the Metro-North Commuter Railroad Company\noperates.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect immediately; provided however, that the\namendments to subparagraph 2 of paragraph (a) of subdivision 1 of\nsection 1263 of the public authorities law made by section ne of this\nact shall not effect the expiration of such paragraph and shall be\ndeemed expired within.\n",
